# SolvaPay Product Vocabulary

## Deprecated terms

Do not mention the following SolvaPay product names in plans, skills, docs, marketing copy, code comments, anchor articles, trademark lists, roadmaps, or any user-facing artifact:

- **MCP Pay** -- retired product name. The live product is **Managed MCP**. Do not propose features, upsell paths, routing, or any new mentions of the old name.

## When you encounter existing mentions

- If you are already editing the file: remove the mention as part of your change.
- If you are not editing the file: flag it for cleanup but do not silently rewrite unrelated files.

## What to suggest instead

When a user's intent matches no-code MCP monetization (paste a server URL, gate tools without code, console setup), route to **Managed MCP** — the provider console path with docs at `/no-code-mcp/overview` and `/no-code-mcp/quick-start`. When they want to write MCP paywall code (greenfield worker, OpenAPI→MCP, SDK wiring), route to the code-based path (`solvapay/create-mcp-app` skill, `create-solvapay` package, or `solvapay/sdk-integration`).

## Canonical product type names

The no-code MCP product type is **Managed MCP** (never Hosted MCP, No-code, or MCP Pay). The code-based type is **SDK**. The canonical product field is `isManagedMcp`; `isMcpPay` remains a deprecated wire alias (accepted on input, emitted on output) for compatibility. Customer-facing surfaces say **MCP server** — the provider's integration method is not the customer's concern.

## Canonical name

The current canonical skill id for the code-based paid-MCP path is `solvapay/create-mcp-app` (directory `skills/create-mcp-app/`). The npm scaffolder is `create-solvapay` (`npm create solvapay -- --type mcp`). Older drafts referenced `create-paid-mcp-app`, `mcp-app`, or split the surface into `openapi-to-mcp` and `building-mcp-app` — all of those are historical.
